{"duration_api_ms":123634,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"942e5ecd-f8fd-4d60-9154-20cb1b66aff3","total_cost_usd":0.194744,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16665,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12808,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16665,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12808,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16665},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12808,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16665,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.194744,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7162,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially a one-parameter curve in flight_path_angle. Every non-dominated point sits at D~3.385, B=1.2, cone=70 (flux 227k to 275k W/m2, bondline T 418 to 391 K). Three limits pin the corner. Mass fraction caps D (margin 2.7e-5 at D=3.3852). The surrogate hull blocks B>1.2 (seven hull failures near this corner). The cone is at its variable bound of 70. Peak g caps steepness at about -3.5702 (margin 1.3e-5). Round 8 gained only 4.5e-5 hypervolume, so almost nothing is left. The remaining options are a marginally larger D and denser gamma coverage.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-844c9143a25c: gamma=-3.5702 gives g=12.0000 (margin 1.26e-5), flux 274550, T 391.08. This is the steep-end corner.\",\"C-6daecae7b30e: gamma=-1.5 (bound) gives flux 227200, T 417.87. This is the shallow-end corner.\",\"D=3.384 gives mass margin 7.356e-4 (C-1120f80f8763) and D=3.3852 gives 2.677e-5 (C-844c9143a25c). The slope of about -0.59/m matches margin proportional to D^2, and extrapolates to a zero at D~3.38525.\",\"C-170baba769f0, C-7113ff857376, C-3d41ce848a30, C-4b1b4e110042: B>1.2 at cone=70 fails the cd_fore hull check. B cannot be raised.\",\"C-1618bda1fac0 and C-94a9f7a46f9b: a smaller D (3.2) gives higher flux and T at similar g, and is dominated. Lowering D to buy gamma headroom costs more T than it gains.\",\"Front points from C-3981896fe111 to C-ecdf516a2040 show smooth, near-linear flux(gamma) and T(gamma). I interpolate between them for the predictions below.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Flux and T fall as ballistic coefficient falls and nose radius rises, which favours large D, high B and large cone, all at their caps. Steeper entry lowers T by about 10 K/deg and raises flux by about 22k W/m2 per deg, while raising peak g by about 1.66 per deg. The g limit therefore fixes the steep end, and the front is the gamma sweep from -1.5 to -3.57. Two improvements remain. Pushing D from 3.3852 to 3.38523 uses up the mass-fraction slack, a tiny gain in flux and T. Filling gaps in the gamma sweep at that D trims the step-like hypervolume loss between neighbouring points. This relies on the Rn^-0.5 heating scaling from prior knowledge as well as on the data.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass-fraction zero-crossing (~3.385245) is extrapolated linearly from two points, so D=3.38523 keeps only about 1e-5 of margin. The g margin at gamma=-3.57025 is very thin, and the small D increase adds roughly 1e-5 g. Expected gains are of order 1e-5 in hypervolume. Predictions are interpolated from neighbouring rows and may be off by a few hundred W/m2 and a few tenths of a K.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-6daecae7b30e\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-end corner with D raised to the mass-fraction limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227190,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.86,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Slightly better than C-6daecae7b30e at the shallow corner of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2af256c14eda\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.6 and -1.65 at the larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.62},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the shallow end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ae2f39f03bd5\",\"rationale\":\"Midpoint of -1.65 and -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231250,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c18b1be3a1fe\",\"rationale\":\"Gap between -1.75 and -1.85.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233330,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.04,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d64a1557f5b6\",\"rationale\":\"Gap between -1.9 and -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236480,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.73,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fa59b50781c\",\"rationale\":\"Gap between -2.0 and -2.15.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238690,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7fa59b50781c\",\"rationale\":\"Second point in the -2.0 to -2.15 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.53,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c3411d095ec3\",\"rationale\":\"Gap between -2.25 and -2.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.72,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2904dca3e864\",\"rationale\":\"Gap between -2.35 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":246730,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.39,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-60b626663373\",\"rationale\":\"Gap between -2.5 and -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250150,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap fill on the front.\",\"requested